# A path written in a recipe's text is keyed by what it names: a file by its content wherever it is, a directory of
# the build by its content, a directory outside the build by its text alone. Each case runs where its host can form
# it and says so where it cannot.
> setupText

# A project header named by absolute, relative and linked spelling; an include directory of the project.
> rebuilds absolute config/a.h
> rebuilds relative config/r.h
> rebuilds linked config/l.h
> rebuilds includedir inc/note.h
# A directory holding one of sbt's targets (project/, the meta-build's), passed as a File: unchanged builds hit. Not
# the project directory itself: scripted keeps sbt's own action cache in it, which every build rewrites.
> steady projectfile
# A directory outside the build named in text is keyed as its text: an edit in it is served from the cache.
> hits hostdir @shared/s.h
# A link inside a project directory to a file outside it, named in text and as an arg part.
> rebuilds linktext @shared/real.h
> rebuilds linkarg @shared/real.h
# A header under sbt's target, named in text and as a File.
> rebuilds gentext @target/gen/g.h
> rebuilds genfile @target/gen/g.h
# Paths holding `'`, folders and files holding several spaces, escaped quotes, a glued operator, escaped spaces.
> rebuilds apostrophe @apostrophe
> rebuilds twospacedir @onedrive/extra.h
> rebuilds twospacefile @bigfile
> rebuilds escapedquote inc/quoted.h
> rebuilds glued inc/glued.h
> rebuilds escapedspace @onedrive/escaped.h
# A header edited at its size and modification time, as a time-preserving copy leaves it.
> rebuildsAtTime sametime same/same.h
# An unreadable directory beneath a named one.
> refusedUnreadable unreadable
# The stated boundaries: a file a response file names, and one through a link out of the build.
> hits response cfg/h.h
> hits linkout @shared/v.h

# Windows spellings of a project header: its drive glued to -I and /FI, rooted on the step's drive, through the
# drive's administrative share, in msys's spelling, upper-cased, and by its 8.3 short name.
> rebuilds driveglued win/w.h
> rebuilds fi win/w.h
> rebuilds rooted win/w.h
> rebuilds unc win/w.h
> rebuilds msys win/w.h
> rebuilds upper win/w.h
> rebuilds shortname @onedrive/short.h

# A link in project/ to sbt's target, which holds the staging: a Matching over project/ leaves the staging out, so
# builds hit.
> linkTarget
> steady targetlink

# What keying costs where a recipe names a host tool; printed for each cell.
> keyTiming

# A project whose target is set to a directory of its own, the directory holding it passed as a File: three builds,
# none refused.
> set target := baseDirectory.value / "app" / "out-custom"
> set probeCase := "customtarget"
> Compile/snxConfig
> Compile/snxConfig
> Compile/snxConfig
